{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "tuning.combat/1",
  "title": "The combat model (work order 009), version 1",
  "description": "Shape of content/tuning/combat.json as of revision 2 (work order 010, scope 1). Every constant the kill-time and win-chance formulas read is a number under constants.<NAME>.value, each with a basis (settled, derived, proposal, open); only CALIBRATION_STEP and RATION_HEAL_HP may be null, the two values the model leaves open (calibration work order; Cooking work order). Both are required keys (Jeremy, answer to work order 010). No 'status' field: the register owns status, as for tuning.xp_curve/1. units.HP_DAMAGE_SCALE is a number. The formulas themselves are prose; they are fixed by this schema version and encoded in scripts/validate/check_combat.py, so a model whose formulas change needs a new schema version. Every other section is free-form prose for the reader.",
